-- ============================================================================
-- DR8 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Completion Design, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). Structure row generated from the tier's manifest.json.
--
-- What this tier owns: the exposed casing program as a first class object,
-- run-in clearance with three verdicts and a stated margin, the through bore
-- as a running minimum with its extents, the four volumes integrated exactly
-- on merged breakpoints, and one module on a real engine defect.
--
-- THE IDEA THE WHOLE TIER RESTS ON. Both fit questions are questions about a
-- PATH and not about a point. A component is checked against the smallest
-- drift anywhere ABOVE it, and a tool is limited by the smallest bore anywhere
-- above its target depth. The published well makes the consequence
-- unmistakable: the safety valve and the side pocket mandrel share an outside
-- diameter of 5.75 in and clear by 0.0704787 and 0.0078486 m respectively, a
-- factor of nine, purely because the valve stops at 153.1 m and the mandrel at
-- 2452.3, which is below the liner top at 2400. The same oversized 6.94 in
-- valve FAILS at 2502.2 m by 0.02237740000000002 and PASSES two hundred metres
-- higher, with nothing about the component changed.
--
-- A SECOND FINDING, IN m03. An EXTREME is not an EXTENT. The published string
-- is advertised at its XN no-go bore of 0.066929 m, and that restriction
-- governs 3.75 m of a 2606.25 m string, a tenth of a percent. The safety valve
-- at 0.06985 governs 2451.6 m, which is 94 percent of it. Ten of the thirteen
-- components have bores that never limit anything at all. A minimum tells you
-- how small and says nothing about how typical, and the fix is four lines of
-- code and no new inputs.
--
-- THE ENGINE DEFECT THIS TIER TEACHES, IN m05, AND WHICH THIS COURSE FOUND.
-- runInClearance ranked its `worst` row by STATUS ALONE, so on any string where
-- every row shares a status, which is every string that PASSES, the reduction
-- degenerated to rows[0]. The published completion reported its first tubing
-- joint at 0.10222865 m against a real tightest row, the production packer, at
-- 0.0046736: a factor of 21.87364130434783 on a string whose margin against the
-- 0.003 m warn threshold is 0.0016736. It was invisible on failing strings and
-- present on exactly the strings whose report is read as reassurance. Nothing
-- caught it because the oracle never computed a worst row, so the golden had no
-- field to compare: the rows were data and the selection was logic, and
-- verifying the first does not verify the second. Fixed upstream as
-- petrolord-engines PR #90 and Suite PR #338, with the oracle now computing it
-- and two guards asserting both the selected row and the 21.87 ratio.
--
-- Every number in the lessons is derived by running the vendored engine; the
-- teaching lab is pinned by completionLab.test.js. Numeric and leakage sweeps
-- over the lessons and the banks are clean.
--
-- Answer keys live only here and in academy_quiz_questions, which has no
-- client SELECT policy.
-- ============================================================================

values ('completion', 'intermediate', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-exposed-program","title":"The Exposed Program","lesson_keys":["l01-what-the-string-runs-through","l02-the-innermost-bore-wins","l03-cuts-merges-and-gaps","l04-governing-drift-to-a-depth"]},{"key":"m02-getting-it-down","title":"Getting It Down","lesson_keys":["l01-run-in-clearance","l02-the-whole-path-above","l03-three-verdicts-and-a-margin","l04-the-packer-through-the-liner","l05-where-an-oversized-item-fails"]},{"key":"m03-getting-through-it-afterwards","title":"Getting Through It Afterwards","lesson_keys":["l01-the-through-bore","l02-cumulative-from-the-top","l03-the-safety-valve-and-the-no-go","l04-an-extreme-is-not-an-extent","l05-what-wireline-access-means"]},{"key":"m04-the-volumes","title":"The Volumes","lesson_keys":["l01-four-volumes","l02-the-annulus-above-the-packer","l03-below-the-packer","l04-breakpoints-not-slices","l05-when-the-integration-skips"]},{"key":"m05-reading-a-check-critically","title":"Reading a Check Critically","lesson_keys":["l01-the-worst-row-was-the-first-row","l02-why-nothing-caught-it","l03-what-the-fix-asserts","l04-what-the-checks-do-not-cover"]},{"key":"m06-the-professional-reading","title":"The Professional Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
